        "original_id": "ca50f235-6bc2-5e70-9a7c-4a5c5da68f6c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Maurice Blanchot, Georges Simenon\n- Works: The Absence of the Book, The Infinite Conversation, The Little Man from Archangel, Jules Maigret\n- Companies: Hamish Hamilton\n- Roles: writer, philosopher, literary theorist\n- Topics: French literature, Belgian literature\n\nFacts:\n- Georges Simenon was born on 13 February 1903 and died on 4 September 1989.\n- Maurice Blanchot was born on 22 September 1907 and died on 20 February 2003.\n- Georges Simenon was a Belgian writer.\n- Maurice Blanchot was a French writer, philosopher, and literary theorist.\n- Georges Simenon published nearly 500 novels and numerous short works.\n- Georges Simenon is best known as the creator of the fictional detective Jules Maigret.\n- The Little Man from Archangel is a novel by Georges Simenon.\n- The Little Man from Archangel was first published in English by Hamish Hamilton in 1957.\n- The Little Man from Archangel has the original title Le Petit Homme d'Arkhangelsk.\n- The Absence of the Book is an essay by Maurice Blanchot.\n- The Absence of the Book appeared in Maurice Blanchot's 1993 collection The Infinite Conversation.",
